cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use WorldPopPy in your work, please cite it as below. This citation
  covers the software only: WorldPopPy is a client and does not provide any
  data. Please also cite the WorldPop datasets you use; their recommended
  citations are given on each dataset's summary page (see the README).
title: "WorldPopPy: A Python client for WorldPop data"
type: software
version: 0.5.1
date-released: 2026-11-22
authors:
  - family-names: Langenbach
    given-names: Sascha
license: MPL-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/lungoruscello/WorldPopPy"
url: "https://worldpoppy.readthedocs.io/"
abstract: >-
  WorldPopPy fetches, merges, and clips raster data from the WorldPop open data
  archive for any area of interest, and returns it as an xarray.DataArray.
  WorldPopPy does not host or provide any data itself; all data is created and
  published by the WorldPop project. WorldPopPy is an independent project and
  is not affiliated with or endorsed by WorldPop.
keywords:
  - WorldPop
  - population
  - raster
  - geospatial
  - xarray
